# Single authority for line endings (2026-11-10 root fix for two classes of line-ending problems:
# Linux server pulls interrupted by local line-ending differences, and Windows autocrlf checking out CRLF
# causing gofmt artifacts and false test failures):
# All text files are stored with unified LF and always checked out as LF (including Windows workspaces) —
# line endings no longer depend on per-platform core.autocrlf settings, and checkout results are byte-identical
# across platforms; pair with `git add --renormalize .` to renormalize existing content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary exemptions (prevent text=auto from misclassifying files and injecting line-ending conversions)
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pem binary
*.zip binary
*.tar.gz binary
